 163:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c **** 
 164:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c **** /**
 165:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @brief  This is a user command used to begin the start-up procedure.
 166:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         If the state machine is in IDLE state the command is executed
 167:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         instantaneously otherwise the command is discarded. User must take
 168:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         care of this possibility by checking the return value.
 169:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         Before calling MCI_StartMotor it is mandatory to execute one of
 170:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         these commands:\n
 171:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         MCI_ExecSpeedRamp\n
 172:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         MCI_ExecTorqueRamp\n
 173:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         MCI_SetCurrentReferences\n
 174:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         Otherwise the behaviour in run state will be unpredictable.\n
 175:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         <B>Note:</B> The MCI_StartMotor command is used just to begin the
 176:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         start-up procedure moving the state machine from IDLE state to
 177:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         IDLE_START. The command MCI_StartMotor is not blocking the execution
 178:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         of project until the motor is really running; to do this, the user
 179:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         have to check the state machine and verify that the RUN state (or
 180:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         any other state) has been reached.
 181:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @param  pHandle Pointer on the component instance to work on.
 182:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @retval bool It returns true if the command is successfully executed
 183:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         otherwise it return false.
 184:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   */
 185:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c **** __weak bool MCI_StartMotor( MCI_Handle_t * pHandle )
