 231:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c **** /**
 232:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @brief  This is a user command used to begin the encoder alignment procedure.
 233:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         If the state machine is in IDLE state the command is executed
 234:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         instantaneously otherwise the command is discarded. User must take
 235:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         care of this possibility by checking the return value.\n
 236:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         <B>Note:</B> The MCI_EncoderAlign command is used just to begin the
 237:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         encoder alignment procedure moving the state machine from IDLE state
 238:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         to IDLE_ALIGNMENT. The command MCI_EncoderAlign is not blocking the
 239:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         execution of project until the encoder is really calibrated; to do
 240:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         this, the user have to check the state machine and verify that the
 241:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         IDLE state has been reached again.
 242:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @param  pHandle Pointer on the component instance to work on.
 243:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   * @retval bool It returns true if the command is successfully executed
 244:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_interface.c ****   *         otherwise it return false.
